GOFusion — license scope
=======================

GOFusion contains code under multiple licenses. The BSD-3-Clause terms below
apply to its original code and documentation, except where separate component
or file terms apply. GOFusion modifications to upstream files follow the
applicable file terms:

* OKVIS2-X: LICENSES/OKVIS2-X-BSD-3-Clause.txt (BSD-3-Clause).

* Supereight2: BSD-3-Clause for the core, with CC0-1.0 and MIT terms for
  files bearing those identifiers. See supereight-2-srl/LICENSES/.
* GSFusion: BSD-3-Clause for the BSD-marked code, with separate
  Gaussian-Splatting terms for the Gaussian model and rendering derivatives.
  See supereight-2-srl/LICENSES/ and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
* MonoGS rasterizer: supereight-2-srl/mono_cuda_rasterizer/LICENSE.md;
  Faster-GS-derived portions also retain their Apache-2.0 terms.
* Faster-GS rasterizer and its adapters:
  supereight-2-srl/fastergs_cuda_rasterizer/LICENSE (Apache-2.0), except the
  NVIDIA helper header, which retains its own BSD notice.
* Other bundled dependencies: their retained licenses and source notices,
  indexed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

The combined application is limited to non-commercial research and evaluation
under the Gaussian-Splatting terms. Other uses require the relevant rights
holders' permission. These terms do not relicense the individual components.
Redistributions must retain the applicable licenses and attribution notices;
DBoW2 additionally requires notification to its original author.
Linked system libraries have separate terms. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for
the SuiteSparse/Gaussian-Splatting binary redistribution compatibility issue.

